{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790420989084,"sessionID":"ses_f22998c3fffepkx1ux7oHrkW17","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_61118f1f7675440b826e95c0","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the /workspace project structure thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The project.godot file contents\n2. The directory structure under scenes/ and scripts/ and global/\n3. Any existing .gd files (especially any Events singleton or similar)\n4. Any existing .tscn files\n\nReturn the full contents of project.godot, list all files recursively, and provide the contents of any existing scripts that might be relevant (especially anything related to Events, autoloads, or UI scenes).","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f22990466ffeu3Fv8PEda3KM29\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a complete report of the `/workspace` project structure.\n\n---\n\n## Full Directory Tree (recursive)\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/\n│   ├── .gdignore                          (empty file)\n│   ├── editor/\n│   │   ├── filesystem_cache10\n│   │   ├── main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg\n│   │   └── project_metadata.cfg\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg      (empty list)\n│   ├── imported/                          (empty)\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg             (empty)\n│   └── uid_cache.bin                      (binary)\n├── global/\n│   ├── events.gd\n│   └── events.gd.uid\n├── scenes/\n│   └── main.tscn\n├── scripts/                               (empty)\n├── project.godot\n└── task_config.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1. `/workspace/project.godot` (full contents)\n\n```ini\n; Engine configuration file.\n; It's best edited using the editor UI and not directly,\n; since the parameters that go here are not all obvious.\n;\n; Format:\n;   [section] ; section goes between []\n;   param=value ; assign values to parameters\n\nconfig_version=5\n\n[application]\n\nconfig/name=\"Battle Over Panel Task\"\nconfig/description=\"Create a battle over screen with buttons and logic\"\nrun/main_scene=\"res://scenes/main.tscn\"\nconfig/features=PackedStringArray(\"4.4\")\n\n[autoload]\n\nEvents=\"*res://global/events.gd\"\n\n[rendering]\n\nrenderer/rendering_method=\"gl_compatibility\"\n```\n\nKey observations:\n- **Project name**: \"Battle Over Panel Task\"\n- **Main scene**: `res://scenes/main.tscn`\n- **Autoloads**: One singleton autoload named `Events`, mapping to `res://global/events.gd`\n- **Renderer**: `gl_compatibility` (Godot 4.4)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Directory Structures\n\n### `scenes/`\n| File | Type |\n|---|---|\n| `main.tscn` | PackedScene (Godot scene) |\n\n### `scripts/`\n**Empty** -- no files exist.\n\n### `global/`\n| File | Type |\n|---|---|\n| `events.gd` | GDScript (autoload singleton) |\n| `events.gd.uid` | UID metadata: `uid://ct11hvse5mkj0` |\n\n---\n\n## 3. All Existing `.gd` Files\n\nThere is exactly **one** `.gd` file in the entire project:\n\n### `/workspace/global/events.gd` (full contents)\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node\n\nsignal battle_over_screen_requested(text: String, type: int)\n```\n\nKey observations:\n- It extends `Node` (standard for autoload singletons).\n- It defines exactly **one signal**: `battle_over_screen_requested(text: String, type: int)`. This is the primary communication mechanism for triggering the battle over screen.\n- There are **no other scripts** in `scripts/` or anywhere else.\n\n---\n\n## 4. All Existing `.tscn` Files\n\nThere is exactly **one** `.tscn` file in the entire project:\n\n### `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` (full contents)\n\n```ini\n[gd_scene format=3 uid=\"uid://d1011main\"]\n\n[node name=\"Main\" type=\"Node\"]\n```\n\nThis is a minimal/barebones scene -- just a root `Node` named \"Main\" with no children, no script, and no configuration beyond its UID.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Task Configuration\n\n### `/workspace/task_config.json` (full contents)\n\n```json\n{\n  \"instruction\": \"Create a battle over UI panel scene and its script. Add res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.tscn with a root Panel named BattleOverPanel, set process mode to Always, and stretch it to full rect. Override the panel style with a StyleBoxFlat using rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.34902). Add a centered VBoxContainer with offsets -20/-20/20/20. Inside it, add a Label named Label with text \\\"Victorious!\\\", centered horizontal and vertical alignment, and LabelSettings font_size 24. Add two Buttons named ContinueButton and RestartButton, each with custom_minimum_size (50, 16), size_flags_horizontal set to expand fill, and texts \\\"Awesome!\\\" and \\\"Restart\\\" respectively. Create res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.gd that class_names BattleOverPanel, defines enum Type {WIN, LOSE}, binds the Label and both Buttons with % paths, connects ContinueButton to get_tree().quit and RestartButton to get_tree().reload_current_scene in _ready, and connects Events.battle_over_screen_requested to show_screen. Implement show_screen(text, type) to update the label text, toggle ContinueButton for WIN and RestartButton for LOSE, show the panel, and pause the scene tree.\"\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Summary\n\nThis is a **fresh Godot 4.4 project** set up as a skeleton for the task described in `task_config.json`. The current state is:\n\n| What exists | Where |\n|---|---|\n| Project config with autoloaded Events singleton | `/workspace/project.godot` |\n| Events singleton (one signal, no logic yet) | `/workspace/global/events.gd` |\n| Empty/unused `scripts/` directory | `/workspace/scripts/` |\n| Bare main scene (just a root `Node`) | `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn` |\n| Task instructions | `/workspace/task_config.json` |\n\nThe task requires creating:\n1. A **new scene** at `res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.tscn` (the `scenes/ui/` directory does not exist yet).\n2. A **new script** at `res://scenes/ui/battle_over_panel.gd` with the `BattleOverPanel` class.\n\nThe existing `Events` singleton in `/workspace/global/events.gd` already declares the signal (`battle_over_screen_requested`) that the new `BattleOverPanel` must connect to. No other scripts or scenes exist in the project.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f22998c3fffepkx1ux7oHrkW17","sessionId":"ses_f22990466ffeu3Fv8PEda3KM29","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790420908958,"end":1790420989075}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_ea9fb547-172c-43c6-b5b3-efb501567b6c"}},"id":"prt_0dd66fb92001tLd3N0h0nlJSx4","sessionID":"ses_f22998c3fffepkx1ux7oHrkW17","messageID":"msg_0dd66c78a001AbqQS2OA6oeow8"}}
